      "problem": "A vertical line $l$ passes through the point $(-6,3).$ Calculate the coordinates of the $x$-intercept of $l.$",
      "worked_solution": "On any vertical line, all points have the same $x$-coordinate.\n\nThe $x$-coordinate of the point $(-6,3)$ is $-6,$ so the $x$-coordinate of the $x$-intercept is also $-6.$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the $x$-intercept are $(-6,0).$",
